\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Choice and update interfaces of the candidate selector. (a) Complete source records ($O=1$) are split at $\kappa $ into profile $P$ and delta $D$. Frozen task and history representations, with public metadata $b(v)$, feed head $g$; the task representation also feeds a candidate-specific residual score. A local sample is sealed as $(j,B,p)$. (b) After target execution, that same assignment $j$ and its independent outcome $Y$ must pass identity, reward-contract, and once-only checks before changing the next residual state. The strips and sampled peer are illustrative; the encoder, head, and updater remain replaceable.}}{4}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:method-state}{{2}{4}{Choice and update interfaces of the candidate selector. (a) Complete source records ($O=1$) are split at $\kappa $ into profile $P$ and delta $D$. Frozen task and history representations, with public metadata $b(v)$, feed head $g$; the task representation also feeds a candidate-specific residual score. A local sample is sealed as $(j,B,p)$. (b) After target execution, that same assignment $j$ and its independent outcome $Y$ must pass identity, reward-contract, and once-only checks before changing the next residual state. The strips and sampled peer are illustrative; the encoder, head, and updater remain replaceable}{figure.caption.8}{}}
